WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:05.910 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  celebrating the war  this video purports to show russian  soldiers dancing before heading to the  front line in ukraine  the video is circulating on several  platforms and has been viewed thousands  of times  but the video isn't from ukraine it  dates from 2018 and shows a uzbekistan  military band at a concert in a  subway using a reverse image search we  found older versions of the video and  were able to locate it with google maps  we come across photos of a subway  station in tashkent uzbekistan not in  russia  ever since russia attacked ukraine  thousands of images and videos of battle  scenes have flooded the internet but be  careful what you share not everything is  real or what it appears to be  these images allegedly show russian jets  launching attacks however  the images are actually from the video  game armor 3.  it is by no means the first time that  such game sequences have been posted and  misused as combat images  we have seen similar examples during the  afghanistan crisis last year  however the case with the following  images is different  here we see a formation of fighter jets  flying over an urban area a twitter user  has written in chinese  live broadcasting of the war in ukraine  the reverse image search of a screenshot  reveals that the video dates back to  2020 and shows an air show north of  moscow  some users are seeking attention by  uploading old videos and sometimes the  media falls for it  this is what happened at the tv branch  of the german media outlet built  the images show hundreds of russian  soldiers allegedly parachuting over the  ukrainian city of kharkiv  as the presenter explains to us  but the footage is old we found the  exact same video on facebook dating back  to 2016.  the footage it appears is from russia  the assault on ukraine is not only  happening from the air but also on the  ground again don't believe everything  you see here  take this tick tock video it shows a  huge explosion allegedly stemming from  an attack in ukraine a day before the  russian invasion began  but what should you make suspicious is  that the trees and bushes are  surprisingly green for february in  ukraine  we also checked for older versions here  and found several narratives of the same  event via reverse image search  the video actually shows a gas station  in the siberian city of novosibirsk that  went up in flames last summer  so again here there is no link to the  war in ukraine  in conflict situations like the current  one between russia and ukraine we  encounter a flood of images on the  internet  some of them are fake so before you  share it's always better to look twice

